# mongot push-mode packages @VERSION@

Install server and clients from the same release. Verify artifacts with SHA256SUMS.
The server archive includes Java and native libraries. See standalone-mongot.md inside the
archive and clients/README.md in the source release for examples.

Search supports cross-index and self-join filters: place `join` in `compound.filter` or
`compound.mustNot`, set `from: "indexName"` (omit for self-joins), `localField`, `foreignField`,
and a foreign `operator`. Both key fields must be strings explicitly mapped as `token`
with matching normalizers. Native typed `_id` keys and foreign-document enrichment are deferred.
See [complete join examples](https://github.com/beardsandbeers/nomongo-t/blob/@COMMIT@/README.md#join-searches-across-indexes)
and join-design-guide.md inside the server archive for limits and lifecycle details.

Python: `python3 -m pip install mongot-standalone-client==@VERSION@`
(or install the included wheel).
Java: unpack `mongot-standalone-client-java-@VERSION@.zip` and use the bundled client JAR.
Node: `npm install ./mongot-standalone-client-@VERSION@.tgz`
Rust: `cargo add mongot-standalone-client@@VERSION@`
(or use the included `.crate` as a vendored dependency).
Docker: `docker pull mybyte/nomongo-t:@VERSION@`

`CatalogService.GetIndexMappings` exports the configured mapping plus observed dynamic types as
static mappings JSON and a complete reusable definition JSON. All four clients support this RPC;
see [the mapping export example](https://github.com/beardsandbeers/nomongo-t/blob/@COMMIT@/clients/README.md#export-a-dynamic-mapping).

`GetIndexStats` and `GetIndexFieldStats` provide document counts, storage averages, and
field storage/memory diagnostics with explicit shared and unknown attribution.

This API manages indexes and pushes BSON to Lucene. Schema updates require reingestion. The
collection-backed 0.2.x API and data directories are incompatible; use a new data directory.
